# URBANPULSE GPS, MAP, SPATIAL INTELLIGENCE & SEVERITY HEATMAP — UNIVERSAL MASTER PROMPT

## Integrated Geospatial Companion to the UrbanPulse AI Civic Intelligence Master Prompt

**Prompt type:** Product-engineering / geospatial implementation master instruction
**Primary purpose:** Build and integrate reliable GPS capture, report geolocation, point-by-point issue mapping, severity heatmaps, spatial aggregation, and map/report synchronization into the existing UrbanPulse application.
**Primary operating area:** Tumakuru (also commonly written as Tumkur), Karnataka, India.
**Primary map modes:** `PINPOINT_REPORT_MAP` and `SEVERITY_HEATMAP`.
**Primary data source:** The existing UrbanPulse report and AI-assessment pipeline.
**Relationship to the AI master prompt:** This prompt consumes and displays the reports, detections, issue identities, severity assessments, priority assessments, verification states, timestamps, and location metadata produced by the separate UrbanPulse AI master prompt. It must not replace, contradict, or silently rewrite that prompt's AI assessment logic.
**Non-negotiable principle:** One real-world issue must remain one traceable issue, even when it is reported many times, detected in many images, seen in many video frames, or displayed in multiple map modes.

