# PART 29 — EDGE-CASE DECISION TABLE

## 137. LOCATION AND MAP EDGE CASES

| Situation | Required behaviour |
|---|---|
| GPS permission denied | Continue report flow; allow manual location if supported; do not invent GPS |
| GPS unavailable | Keep report unlocated and visible in non-map counts |
| GPS accuracy poor | Show approximate marker/uncertainty; avoid false street-level precision |
| GPS timestamp old | Flag stale location; do not silently replace with upload-time GPS |
| User uploads from home | Do not treat upload-time location as issue location without confirmation |
| Screenshot contains civic image | Follow AI relevance policy; do not infer GPS from screenshot pixels |
| Multiple objects in one image | Preserve individual detections; do not fabricate per-object world coordinates |
| Same issue reported by many users | Use confirmed physical issue identity; one issue-level point with multiple report references |
| Nearby but distinct potholes | Keep separate physical issues unless confirmed association exists |
| Many markers overlap | Cluster/stack visually; do not modify source coordinates |
| No severity score | Neutral grey; do not assume low severity |
| Issue resolved | Apply status filter; do not recolour it as low severity |
| High-severity issue in sparse cell | Cell must be red under the default maximum-severity rule |
| Empty cell | No-data styling, not green |
| No official ward data | Do not show fabricated ward layer |
| Outside Tumakuru boundary | Preserve point and label jurisdiction appropriately |
| Heatmap API unavailable | Use supported alternative; do not silently show fake blur |
| Map tiles fail | Keep data, show map failure state, do not delete reports |
| Geocoder returns city only | Store city-level approximate label, not exact street position |
| AI reports low confidence but severity high | Keep detection confidence and severity distinct; apply configured review policy |
| Map refresh occurs | Do not duplicate features or reset user context |

